#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
FEDERAL BANK DOCUMENT AI - Aadhaar masking for account-opening PDFs
Engines: PaddleOCR + OpenCV + your trained RF-DETR.

In every case the LAST 4 DIGITS stay visible:   1234 5678 9012  ->  XXXX XXXX 9012
The QR code is blacked out completely.

1. Aadhaar number typed/printed in the form
      PaddleOCR reads the page. A 12-digit number is masked when it
        - passes Verhoeff, or
        - sits next to an Aadhaar / Aadhar / UID label, or
        - is written in the 4-4-4 Aadhaar grouping.

2. Aadhaar number written by hand (OpenCV, no handwriting OCR needed)
      Printed text and ruling lines are removed, what is left is the pen ink.
      Ink digits are grouped into rows. A row is masked when
        - it has 10-14 digits and sits next to an Aadhaar label, or
        - it has exactly 12 digits arranged 4-4-4 (two wider gaps).

3. Aadhaar card image embedded in / photographed on the PDF page
      Your RF-DETR model (AADHAAR_NUMBER + QR classes) runs on every embedded
      image AND on the whole page (tiled), at 0/90/180/270 degrees so sideways
      cards are handled. Number -> last 4 kept, QR -> black.

Full numbers are never written to the report.

Run:
    python main.py                                  (process every PDF in input/Files)
    python main.py input/fedtest.pdf
    python main.py input/fedtest.pdf --debug          (print model detections)
    python main.py input/fedtest.pdf --threshold 0.15 (model misses cards)
    python main.py input/fedtest.pdf --tile 0         (faster, whole page only)
"""

